      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T12:45:00Z",
      "note": "The attacker EOA sent eight Blast transactions; the anchor is the exploit-contract creation and the only one that touches the vault. Netting the receipt shows the vault paying WETH and rYOLO to the attacker contract against BZR burned from a third-party holder, which is the exit executed on someone else\u2019s position. The vault is not upgradeable: identical runtime code hash at the deployment block 4573443 and at block 4619716, EIP-1967 slot zero, so the exploited code is 1.07 days old and its deployer 0x1cfecded895d851f16a39e1bc85d9196ee92021f is not an attacker address. rYOLO has no DefiLlama price series so its component carries quantity only and the USD figure is the WETH leg alone."
    }
